From 800128d9729c01aa597dd5c70689a0e3e55ee03b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:26:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] test(privacy): restored pages, other tabs and handoff
 waits in a real browser

Adds 39 checks to the privacy section of
scripts/e2e/music-world-continuity.e2e.mjs for audit findings A3 and A4.

- Handoff: never answered (ten seconds, then both answers), the member's
  own record answering in place, a member with no record, a page that
  reloads signed in, and a refused handoff. A watcher installed before
  any script of the page keeps the first moment the page was open to a
  visitor who had not agreed. There must be none.
- Restore: Go back then the browser's Forward, and the policy link, Agree,
  then the browser's Back, against a real back/forward cache. Playwright's
  headless shell has no such cache and Playwright switches it off besides,
  so these run in a second browser, the full Chromium, started only when
  they are reached.
- Go back with nothing behind the entry, and a step back that stays in
  the same document.
- Agreement given in another tab of the same site (the storage event) and
  on another McCluster host (the shared cookie, read when the browser
  gives the tab focus again).

Against the gate as it was before the previous commit, 19 of these checks
fail and the suite stops at the first: "handoff wait: the page is behind
the wall from its first paint".

